Task: Render town from data — Kenney track tiles as road grid, houses on lots, park corner, hydrants/poles (visual; manual verify: layout matches authored map, no z-fighting)

Summary of changes:
- src/game/town/townBuilder.ts: buildTown(grid) walks the map and returns
  { group, dispose }. Per tile it emits a ground decal (lot green / lighter
  park green) plus, for roads, a road surface and one lane marking per
  connected neighbour — so the derived track-piece shape is legible. Houses
  are body + 4-sided roof cone + door on the local +z wall, rotated by
  yawForDirection(facing) so the authored facing is visible and testable.
  Props are hydrant (barrel + cap), power pole (post + crossbar), and tree
  (trunk + cone foliage), placed from the map's kerbside offsets. All
  meshes are named (road-x-y, house-id-body, hydrant-1-barrel...) for
  debugging. Geometry is shared (one unit plane/box/cylinder/cone) and
  scaled per instance; materials are cached per colour.
- src/game/scene.ts: the scene is now a stage only (sky, fog, daylight) —
  the town owns the ground. Daylight has a shadow-casting sun (1024 map,
  +-8 unit ortho shadow frustum, normal bias) and a shadow cleanup path.
- src/main.ts: enables shadow mapping (PCFShadowMap) and mounts the built
  town into the scene.
- src/game/camera.ts: temporary whole-town framing (VIEW_HEIGHT 9) and a
  closer camera position, since orthographic framing ignores distance but
  fog and depth precision do not. The CameraRig task replaces this.
- src/game/scene.test.ts, src/game/town/townBuilder.test.ts: 10 new tests
  (48 total) covering tile/house/prop placement against the authored map,
  lane markings per road connection, single shared geometry per kind,
  facing yaws, shadow flags, and teardown.

Verification (visual task — manual verification per workflow.md):
- Automated: pnpm check clean, pnpm typecheck clean, CI=true pnpm test
  → 6 files / 48 tests; coverage 99.2% statements (scene 100%,
  townBuilder 99%).
- Manual, production preview build (port 4173, SW cache cleared first):
  the rendered town matches the authored map — perimeter ring road with
  white lane markings plus the north-south cross street at x3, ten houses
  on their lots with doors facing their road, the lighter park corner with
  two trees, four kerbside hydrants and three power poles. Two bugs were
  found and fixed by looking: (1) the whole frame was fog-washed because
  the ortho camera sat ~36 units from town centre while fog was ranged for
  the old 240-unit ground — camera moved to ~10 units and fog re-ranged;
  (2) three 0.186 removed PCFSoftShadowMap (console warning) — switched to
  PCFShadowMap.
- Z-fighting: verified clean layering of ground (y=0), road (y=0.02) and
  markings (y=0.035) with no speckling at any zoom in the preview.
- Shadows verified by temporarily lowering the sun: house, tree, pole and
  hydrant shadows all appear; final sun angle (12,10,9) chosen for the
  toy-diorama look with hemisphere fill at 1.1.

Follow-ups: real Kenney models replace the primitive stand-ins in the asset
pipeline task, and the CameraRig replaces the whole-town framing.
